# You usually do NOT need to place anything here: the Docker build's `models`
# stage auto-fetches buffalo_l (det_10g.onnx + w600k_r50.onnx) and bakes them
# into the image. See ../Dockerfile.
#
# Put files here ONLY if you want to override the auto-fetched models — that
# requires re-enabling the bind mount in server/docker-compose.yml
# (./face-service-rust/models:/app/models), which shadows the baked-in copy.
#
# Required names (InsightFace buffalo_l):
#   det_10g.onnx     (SCRFD-10GF detector)
#   w600k_r50.onnx   (wbob glint360k/w600k recognition, 512-d)
# Grab them manually from ~/.insightface/models/buffalo_l/ or the release pack:
#   https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface/releases/download/v0.7/buffalo_l.zip
#
# These two are preserved from the retired Python service and are NOT used by
# the current Rust /verify (passthrough liveness); kept for the future
# MiniFAS anti-spoof port. See ../src/main.rs crate header:
#   best_model_quantized.onnx  (MiniFAS liveness)
#   detector_quantized.onnx    (MiniFAS face detector)
